    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0384" n="372" xml:id="pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/75: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-25T09:00:00-00:44">March 25, 1942—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. From McBride for Villard. If agreement is not yet approved please phone John
                    Martyn, assistant to Secretary of War and ask him to give the Secretary
                    following personal message from me: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>I would be grateful if War Department could approve agreement with
                            Liberia which I have negotiated and inform Department of State. Delay is
                            weakening our position here. Many thanks.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> [McBride] <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
